{"text": "Jamie =\n\nTopsfield, MA\n\n(202) 642-4959\n\na\nBelsito -\ninfo@belsitoforcongress.com\n\nProfile\n\nAchievements:\n\nExperience\n\nEducation\n\nWebsite:\nbelsitoforcongress.com\n\nDemocratic Candidate for the Sixth Congressional District. Mother, progressive leader,\neducation activist, mental health advocate, policy expert, women\u2019s rights champion, wife.\n\nAdvocated on Capitol Hill for the Successful Passage of the Following Bills:\nH.R. 1318: \u201cPreventing Maternal Deaths Act of 2018\"\nH.R. 3235: Congresswoman Katherine Clark's \"Bringing Postpartum Depression Out of the\nShadows Act of 2015\" [21st Century Cures Act]\nH.R. 5291: \"Safe Medications for Moms and Babies Act\"\nH.R. 5065: \"BABES Act\" Bottles and Breastfeeding Equipment Screening Act\nAmerican Competitiveness and Workforce Improvement Act\nAmerican Competitiveness in the 21 Century Act\nSpousal Work Permits for L1 Visa Holders\n\nFounder, Maternal Mental Health Leadership Alliance \u2014 2018-Present\nCreated the only advocacy organization in the nation dedicated to achieving positive maternal\nmental health policies on Capital Hill. Ended TSA's rules on disposing breast milk on flights.\nMade postpartum care part of the ACA. Got funding for states to study why women of color\ndie at disproportionately high levels during childbirth in this nation.\n\nHR Executive, 2001-2006, 2008-2009\nLed immigration programs and international deployment initiatives for major international\ncompanies, including: AOL, Raytheon, and Philips.\n\nFederal lobbyist, American Council on International Personnel \u2014 2006-2008\nPartnered with coalitions to craft business immigration reform and legislation.\nWorked with Senator Ted Kennedy\u2019s office to formulate the H-1B1 Visa Program, spousal\nwork permit opportunities, and American workforce retraining programs.\n\nCongressional Intern, Congressman Joe Moakley \u2014 1996-1997\nFacilitated immigration cases for families in the district who wanted their loved ones to be\nreunited in this country. Helped reduce the district\u2019s 20-year backlog of cases.\n\nSalem State College \u2014 BA, political science 1996\nReading Memorial High School \u2014 1991",
